---
import sql from '../../backend/calories/setup.sql?raw';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/calories/icon.svg" />
    <title>Connect your private journal · Calories</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <a class="back" href="/calories/">← Back to Calories</a>
      <p class="eyebrow">ONE-TIME SETUP</p>
      <h1>A home for your journal.</h1>
      <p class="intro">Calories runs on your website. Your password and food records live in your own Supabase project, with access limited to your account.</p>
      <ol>
        <li><h2>Create a Supabase project</h2><p>Open the <a href="https://supabase.com/dashboard" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Supabase dashboard</a> and create a project. Choose a region near you. Check the plan and cost shown before confirming.</p></li>
        <li><h2>Create your account</h2><p>In <strong>Authentication → Users → Add user</strong>, create your email/password account and mark the email confirmed. Copy its User UID. Disable <strong>Allow new users to sign up</strong> in the authentication settings. Keep email/password sign-in enabled.</p><p>Choose the password in Supabase. It never goes into the website source.</p></li>
        <li><h2>Protect the database</h2><p>The SQL below is configured for your account in the <strong>calories</strong> project. Copy it and run the entire script in the Supabase SQL Editor. Keep the <code>private</code> schema out of the API’s exposed schemas. This creates the tracker table and access policies; it preserves data if rerun for the same owner.</p><div class="sql-tools"><button id="copy-sql" type="button">Copy SQL</button><a href="/calories/setup.sql" download>Download SQL</a><span id="copy-status" role="status"></span></div><details><summary>View the complete SQL setup</summary><pre id="setup-sql">{sql}</pre></details><p class="verify">Then run the <a href="/calories/verify.sql" download>database verification SQL</a> to check the permissions, 30-day expiry, and conflict protection. Its temporary test changes are rolled back.</p></li>
        <li><h2>Open Calories</h2><p>Your project URL and public publishable key are already configured. Return to <a href="/calories/">Calories</a> and sign in with your email and password. Both devices use the same database automatically.</p><p>Use only a public publishable key. A secret or service-role key can bypass the access policies and must stay private.</p></li>
        <li><h2>Optional connection overrides</h2><p>To change the built-in project connection later, add public values to the GitHub repository’s <strong>Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → Variables</strong>:</p><ul><li><code>PUBLIC_CALORIES_SUPABASE_URL</code></li><li><code>PUBLIC_CALORIES_SUPABASE_KEY</code></li></ul><p>Run the Deploy to GitHub Pages workflow again. For local development, copy <code>.env.example</code> to <code>.env</code> and enter the same public values. You can also enter them separately on each device using the app’s connection screen.</p></li>
      </ol>
      <aside><h2>Day to day</h2><p>Add foods using the nutrition label and its reference quantity, such as 100 g or 1 piece. Log portions against the same raw/cooked state as the label. Energy is calculated from protein, carbohydrate, and fat; portions and macros scale automatically. Past entries retain their nutrition values when a food changes.</p><p>The initial burned-calorie, deficit, and protein values match your spreadsheet. You can change them for a day or as defaults.</p><p>“Remember this device” saves the session for up to 30 days from sign-in. Without it, the session is kept in this browser tab. Signing out clears this device’s session. The database also rejects revoked or expired sessions.</p><p>On iPhone, use Safari’s <strong>Share → Add to Home Screen</strong> for quick access. On Mac, bookmark <code>fangxk2003.github.io/calories/</code>. An internet connection is required for sign-in and saving; the app reports unsaved changes and offers JSON backups.</p></aside>
      <p class="sources">Technical details: <a href="https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/postgres/row-level-security">Supabase access policies</a>, <a href="https://supabase.com/docs/guides/auth/sessions">sessions</a>, and <a href="https://supabase.com/docs/guides/getting-started/api-keys">public API keys</a>.</p>
    </main>
    <script>
      const button = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#copy-sql');
      button?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        const status = document.querySelector('#copy-status');
        try {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(document.querySelector('#setup-sql')?.textContent ?? '');
          if (status) status.textContent = 'Copied. Run the entire script in your calories project.';
        } catch { if (status) status.textContent = 'Use Download SQL, or select and copy the text below.'; }
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
<style>
  :global(*) { box-sizing: border-box; }
  :global(body) { margin: 0; color: #25382e; background: #f7f6f1; font: 16px/1.7 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif; }
  main { max-width: 800px; padding: 40px 24px 72px; margin: auto; }
  a { color: #285b46; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .back { font-size: 14px; text-decoration: none; }
  .eyebrow { margin: 48px 0 8px; letter-spacing: .14em; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(32px, 6vw, 46px); line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -.045em; margin: 0 0 20px; }
  h2 { font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.3; letter-spacing: -.02em; margin: 0 0 12px; }
  .intro { color: #667267; font-size: 18px; }
  ol { padding-left: 28px; margin-top: 38px; }
  ol > li { padding: 0 0 28px 10px; }
  li::marker { font-weight: 700; }
  p { margin: 0 0 12px; }
  code { background: #eaece2; padding: 2px 5px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 13px; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .sql-tools { display: flex; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 14px; margin: 20px 0 12px; }
  button { border: 0; background: #244a3c; color: #fff; font: inherit; border-radius: 9px; padding: 10px 16px; cursor: pointer; }
  #copy-status { color: #667267; font-size: 12px; width: 100%; }
  details { border: 1px solid #dfe3d6; background: white; border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px; }
  .verify { margin-top: 16px; font-size: 14px; }
  summary { cursor: pointer; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; }
  pre { max-height: 400px; overflow: auto; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6; padding-top: 16px; }
  aside { padding: 28px; background: #eaf0e5; border-radius: 14px; }
  .sources { margin-top: 28px; font-size: 13px; color: #667267; }
</style>
